//
// @PLN153 phase 1 — the REFUSE half of @FR-N-Domain's pair: sqrt is float?, so a float slot refuses it undischarged.
//
// The pair exists so the citation at the rule's home is a receipt for a measured
// refusal, not a comment: `rule_tags.py check` counts the citation, this file is what
// makes it honest.  Its expectation is the diagnostic's own text, pinned as a substring.
//
// @falsified-at: 8498fdf1 → here (hand-measured, a warning-only channel): the parent build
//   refuses the program outright (`cannot change type from float to float?`).
//   HOLDS: on --interpret, assertions, leak, panic, free-refusal, expectations are equal on
//   both trees, measured by `scripts/falsify.sh --bulk` against 8498fdf1; falsify prints only
//   the channels that MOVE, and requires HERE to be clean, so each of those is clean on both.
//   The exit channel carries this one on that backend. The native side was not scored in that
//   run.
// @EXPECT_WARNING: a nullable `float?` is stored into the local `z` of the non-null type `float`
fn f(y: float) -> float { z: float = sqrt(y); return z; }
fn main() {
  assert(f(4.0) == 2.0 && f(-1.0) == null, "the root, or null out of the domain: {f(4.0)} {f(-1.0)}");
  println("domain reported");
}
